    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The region of Bradford was part of the traditional territory of the Narragansett people prior to European arrival.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bradford_rhode_island"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bradford thrived as a colonial settlement from the 1730s through the early 1900s before its gradual decline.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://unitedstatesghosttowns.com/bradford-rhode-island-ghost-town/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Bradford Village Historic District was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1996.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bradford%2C_Rhode_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Economic factors like the closure of sawmills, gristmills, and textile operations contributed to the abandonment of Bradford.",
